WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.747 --> 00:00:03.708
Could Barbie ever have been uncontroversial?

00:00:03.708 --> 00:00:04.708
I don't think so

00:00:04.708 --> 00:00:09.052
Because for the past fifty years, femininity has been a contested space

00:00:10.494 --> 00:00:13.825
In the past, dolls had all been baby dolls

00:00:14.462 --> 00:00:17.528
They had all been about teaching little girls how to nurture

00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:20.556
Barbie was a wildly revolutionary toy

00:00:22.024 --> 00:00:24.857
Barbie became things that real women hadn't become

00:00:25.403 --> 00:00:26.533
She had broken barriers

00:00:27.612 --> 00:00:31.354
These dolls enable girls to tell stories about dreams

00:00:31.688 --> 00:00:36.548
She's been around 55 years, but the last few years have been trying for Barbie

00:00:37.795 --> 00:00:39.484
Barbie was everything we didn't want to be...

00:00:39.484 --> 00:00:40.784
...and were being told to be

00:00:41.226 --> 00:00:44.370
Some people think Barbie needs to be liberated

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.528
You look at television and film and music...

00:00:48.528 --> 00:00:50.971
... and you see the same body type being idealized

00:00:51.387 --> 00:00:54.324
Perception of Barbie is that she's vapid, materialistic...

00:00:54.324 --> 00:00:55.569
...and she's not healthy for girls

00:00:55.751 --> 00:01:01.118
This limited understanding of who girls are is not acceptable

00:01:02.418 --> 00:01:06.715
We have to make such a drastic shift, to get people to care about Barbie

00:01:07.911 --> 00:01:12.097
The overall problem is being judged by our outsides, not our insides

00:01:12.513 --> 00:01:18.103
It starts with just changing the ideals that we set forward as what a normal body looks like

00:01:20.807 --> 00:01:24.603
Feminism, and how a girl sees herself, and self-esteem for girls

00:01:25.045 --> 00:01:31.623
To put that all on the tiny plastic shoulders of a doll is quite a burden

00:01:31.575 --> 00:01:35.215
I don't think I've ever been involved with something as culturally significant as this

00:01:36.671 --> 00:01:38.907
We're taking a really big step forward

00:01:43.899 --> 00:01:46.510
I don't want Barbie to be history

